{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:4892-1","published":"2026-10-23T10:48:07Z","modified":"2026-10-24T17:23:10.297365390Z","related":["CVE-2022-50578","CVE-2023-54158","CVE-2023-54180","CVE-2025-68358","CVE-2026-43299","CVE-2026-63948","CVE-2026-63983","CVE-2026-64012","CVE-2026-64280","CVE-2026-64422","CVE-2026-64456","CVE-2026-64593","CVE-2026-68106","CVE-2026-68233","CVE-2026-68236","CVE-2026-68303","CVE-2026-68323","CVE-2026-68430","CVE-2026-72015","CVE-2026-72236","CVE-2026-72319","CVE-2026-72476","CVE-2026-72493","CVE-2026-74408","CVE-2026-74544","CVE-2026-74578","CVE-2026-74583","CVE-2026-74587","CVE-2026-74653","CVE-2026-74675","CVE-2026-80977","CVE-2026-89542","CVE-2026-89726","CVE-2026-89778","CVE-2026-89987","CVE-2026-90011","CVE-2026-90283","CVE-2026-93252","CVE-2026-93287","CVE-2026-93800","CVE-2026-93820","CVE-2026-93822","CVE-2026-97416","CVE-2026-97491","CVE-2026-98010","CVE-2026-98077","CVE-2026-98130","CVE-2026-98252","CVE-2026-98269","CVE-2026-98347","CVE-2026-98354","CVE-2026-98357","CVE-2026-98358","CVE-2026-98359","CVE-2026-98365","CVE-2026-99999"],"upstream":["CVE-2022-50578","CVE-2023-54158","CVE-2023-54180","CVE-2025-68358","CVE-2026-43299","CVE-2026-63948","CVE-2026-63983","CVE-2026-64012","CVE-2026-64280","CVE-2026-64422","CVE-2026-64456","CVE-2026-64593","CVE-2026-68106","CVE-2026-68233","CVE-2026-68236","CVE-2026-68303","CVE-2026-68323","CVE-2026-68430","CVE-2026-72015","CVE-2026-72236","CVE-2026-72319","CVE-2026-72476","CVE-2026-72493","CVE-2026-74408","CVE-2026-74544","CVE-2026-74578","CVE-2026-74583","CVE-2026-74587","CVE-2026-74653","CVE-2026-74675","CVE-2026-80977","CVE-2026-89542","CVE-2026-89726","CVE-2026-89778","CVE-2026-89987","CVE-2026-90011","CVE-2026-90283","CVE-2026-93252","CVE-2026-93287","CVE-2026-93800","CVE-2026-93820","CVE-2026-93822","CVE-2026-97416","CVE-2026-97491","CVE-2026-98010","CVE-2026-98077","CVE-2026-98130","CVE-2026-98252","CVE-2026-98269","CVE-2026-98347","CVE-2026-98354","CVE-2026-98357","CVE-2026-98358","CVE-2026-98359","CVE-2026-98365","CVE-2026-99999"],"summary":"Security update for the Linux Kernel","details":"\nThe SUSE Linux Enterprise 12 SP5 kernel was updated to fix various security issues:\n\nThe following security issues were fixed:\n\n- CVE-2023-54158: btrfs: don't free qgroup space unless specified (bsc#1256076).\n- CVE-2023-54180: btrfs: handle case when repair happens with dev-replace (bsc#1255995).\n- CVE-2025-68358: btrfs: fix racy bitfield write in btrfs_clear_space_info_full() (bsc#1255531).\n- CVE-2026-43299: btrfs: do not ASSERT() when the fs flips RO inside btrfs_repair_io_failure() (bsc#1264851).\n- CVE-2026-63948: Bluetooth: L2CAP: fix chan ref leak in l2cap_chan_timeout() on !conn (bsc#1272670).\n- CVE-2026-63983: net: Introduce skb tc depth field to track packet loops (bsc#1273040).\n- CVE-2026-64012: net/sched: sch_sfb: Replace direct dequeue call with peek and qdisc_dequeue_peeked (bsc#1273764).\n- CVE-2026-64280: fpga: dfl-afu: validate DMA mapping length in afu_dma_map_region() (bsc#1273599).\n- CVE-2026-64422: net: ipv4: bound TCP reordering sysctl writes and MTU probe sizes (bsc#1273290).\n- CVE-2026-64456: hwrng: virtio: clamp device-reported used.len at copy_data() (bsc#1273288).\n- CVE-2026-64593: btrfs: do not trim a device which is not writeable (bsc#1274497).\n- CVE-2026-68106: drm/amdgpu: fix division by zero with invalid uvd dimensions (bsc#1274853).\n- CVE-2026-68233: drm/vc4: Shut down BO cache timer before teardown (bsc#1275644).\n- CVE-2026-68236: drm/amd/display: set new_stream to NULL after release (bsc#1275659).\n- CVE-2026-68303: drm/vc4: hvs/v3d: Fix null dereference in unbind (bsc#1275080).\n- CVE-2026-68323: tipc: serialize udp bearer replicast list updates (bsc#1274653).\n- CVE-2026-68430: drm/amdgpu/gfx8: drop unecessary BUG_ON() (bsc#1276273).\n- CVE-2026-72015: fs/resctrl: Fix double-add of pseudo-locked region's RMID to free list (bsc#1276791).\n- CVE-2026-72236: s390/perf_cpum_cf: Add missing array_index_nospec() to __hw_perf_event_init() (bsc#1277614).\n- CVE-2026-72319: ipvs: ensure inner headers in ICMP errors are in headroom (bsc#1275964).\n- CVE-2026-72476: dmaengine: Fix possible use after free (bsc#1276844).\n- CVE-2026-72493: net: serialize netif_running() check in enqueue_to_backlog() (bsc#1276951).\n- CVE-2026-74408: wifi: ath9k: fix OOB access from firmware tx status queue ID (bsc#1276387).\n- CVE-2026-74544: net/sched: cls_u32: validate offshift to prevent shift-out-of-bounds (bsc#1277894).\n- CVE-2026-74578: crypto: algif_skcipher - force synchronous processing on trees without ctx->state (bsc#1275564).\n- CVE-2026-74583: net/sched: cls_route: fix fastmap use-after-free on filter (bsc#1277889).\n- CVE-2026-74587: sctp: fix use-after-free of cached ASCONF chunk (bsc#1277821).\n- CVE-2026-74653: serial: 8250_of: clear stuck empty-FIFO RX-timeout on LPC32xx (bsc#1277310).\n- CVE-2026-74675: vt: stabilize tty reference in kbd_keycode with tty_port_tty_get (bsc#1278313).\n- CVE-2026-80977: net: skbuff: don't touch shared zerocopy state in skb_tx_error() (bsc#1280259).\n- CVE-2026-89542: SUNRPC: harden gss_krb5_unwrap_v2 against short tokens (bsc#1280387).\n- CVE-2026-89726: lib/ucs2_string.c: fix out-of-bounds read in ucs2_strnlen() (bsc#1281058).\n- CVE-2026-89778: isofs: fix out-of-bounds page array access on empty zisofs block (bsc#1280966).\n- CVE-2026-89987: mm/huge_memory: transfer the pmd dirty bit to the folio on zap (bsc#1281819).\n- CVE-2026-90011: scsi: target: iscsi: Reserve a terminator byte for the login payload (bsc#1281280).\n- CVE-2026-90283: hugetlbfs: release subpool on fill_super failure (bsc#1281771).\n- CVE-2026-93252: ocfs2: make ocfs2_set_acl() static (bsc#1282784).\n- CVE-2026-93287: i2c: smbus: reject oversized block transfers in the common path (bsc#1282744).\n- CVE-2026-93800: btrfs: fix use-after-free on reloc root after error in insert_dirty_subvol() (bsc#1282808).\n- CVE-2026-93820: PCI: rockchip: Protect root bus removal with rescan lock (bsc#1282755).\n- CVE-2026-93822: PCI: iproc: Protect root bus removal with rescan lock (bsc#1282762).\n- CVE-2026-97416: btrfs: balance: fix potential bg lookup failure in btrfs_may_alloc_data_chunk() (bsc#1282770).\n- CVE-2026-97491: net/rds: Don't sleep inside rds_ib_conn_path_shutdown (bsc#1283142).\n- CVE-2026-98010: net/sched: drr: clamp quantum in change class (bsc#1283823).\n- CVE-2026-98077: netfilter: nf_conntrack_sip: fix OOB read in sip_skip_whitespace() (bsc#1283979).\n- CVE-2026-98130: sctp: fix a TOCTOU race in SCTP_CMD_TIMER_START (bsc#1283835).\n- CVE-2026-98252: RDMA/core: fix refcount bug in iwpm_get_nlmsg_request() (bsc#1284581).\n- CVE-2026-98269: btrfs: abort transaction on failure to update inode for hole punching and reflinking (bsc#1284606).\n- CVE-2026-98347: IB/IPoIB: Avoid restoring OPER_UP after multicast flush (bsc#1284295).\n- CVE-2026-98354: RDMA/mad: Fix receive buffer leak when PKey enforcement fails (bsc#1284291).\n- CVE-2026-98357: IB/isert: wait for deferred control PDU completions before releasing the connection (bsc#1284791).\n- CVE-2026-98358: IB/iser: reject a remote invalidation of an unregistered direction (bsc#1284289).\n- CVE-2026-98359: RDMA/core: Reject unregistering netdevs in ib_get_eth_speed (bsc#1284746).\n- CVE-2026-98365: RDMA/rxe: Fix integer overflow in mr_check_range() leading to OOB access (bsc#1284288).\n- CVE-2026-99999: ipv4: validate checksum_start before completing checksum (bsc#1285684).\n\nThe following non security issues were fixed:\n\n- kernel-binary.spec.in: Emulate kabi.pl error when suse-kabi-tools is used.\n- net: add inline function skb_csum_is_sctp (bsc#1285684).\n- netfilter: nfnetlink_queue: unbreak SCTP traffic (bsc#1285684).\n- vc_screen: reload vc pointer before if (ret) in vcs_write() to avoid UAF (git-fixes).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel-default","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Live Patching 12 SP5","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/kernel-default&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Live%20Patching%2012%20SP5"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.12.14-122.336.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"kernel-default-kgraft":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kernel-default-kgraft-devel":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kgraft-patch-4_12_14-122_336-default":"1-8.3.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4892-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kgraft-patch-SLE12-SP5_Update_89","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Live Patching 12 SP5","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/kgraft-patch-SLE12-SP5_Update_89&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Live%20Patching%2012%20SP5"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1-8.3.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"kernel-default-kgraft":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kernel-default-kgraft-devel":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kgraft-patch-4_12_14-122_336-default":"1-8.3.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4892-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-default","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server 12 SP5-LTSS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/kernel-default&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%2012%20SP5-LTSS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.12.14-122.336.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"cluster-md-kmp-default":"4.12.14-122.336.1","dlm-kmp-default":"4.12.14-122.336.1","gfs2-kmp-default":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kernel-default":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kernel-default-base":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kernel-default-devel":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kernel-default-man":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kernel-devel":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kernel-macros":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kernel-source":"4.12.14-122.336.1","kernel-syms":"4.12.14-122.336.1","ocfs2-kmp-default":"4.12.14-122.336.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4892-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-source","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server 12 SP5-LTSS","p